      "message": "@gregkh@google.com, I was talking to our team about how to clean these changes up.\n\nIn the 13-5.15 change, there were really 2 changes: one to disable the KABI_RESERVE macros, and one to disable the {VENDOR,OEM}_DATA macros. We should\u0027ve split into two distinct changes. The android-mainline change is just the {VENDOR,OEM}_DATA macros. I\u0027m not sure why init/init_task.c and kernel/fork.c changes weren\u0027t there. IMO, it should\u0027ve been. I suspect it wasn\u0027t caught in initial testing but I see it got fixed separately in commit 78d6de78638b6.\n\nFor the sake of android-mainline and future releases, I think this change makes sense as-is but the cherry-picks on the other branches make the context of this change more confusing. Should we make it a new change-id to help clear up the confusion?",
